# Copy this file to `backend/.env` and fill in a real key. `.env` is gitignored.
#
# The 5 detective agents are served by OpenRouter (an OpenAI-API-compatible aggregator).
# Without this key the HTTP API still starts and Mr. X can still move - the server boots and
# serves the whole SPA - but starting a round is refused with a 503 naming this variable
# (server.py checks before opening the stream, since a failure inside it cannot send a status
# code).
#
# Get a key at https://openrouter.ai/keys - the model this project uses
# (see backend/scotland_yard/llm_client.py:OPENROUTER_MODEL) is inexpensive, but note that one
# full round costs roughly 30 calls: 6 per detective's turn (a proposal, four responses, a
# final decision) across 5 detectives. A complete 24-round game is therefore around 720.
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
